From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opi5 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pci: pcie_dw_rockchip: put the port in reset before the
 OS

The driver trains the link at probe (with CONFIG_PCI_INIT_R, on every
boot) and leaves it that way: the LTSSM running, PERST# released and
the slot powered. The OS then starts with the endpoint live in L0.

The Orange Pi 5 Pro's Motorcomm YT6801 fails to train again under Linux
on about half of such boots (LTSSM stuck in Polling.Compliance) until
its supply is switched off and on. Holding it in reset alone doesn't
help; removing the slot power before the OS does: 14 of 14 boots
trained, against about half without.

Add a remove hook with DM_FLAG_OS_PREPARE, like other PCIe host
drivers have, that asserts PERST#, stops the LTSSM and switches
vpcie3v3 off. A port whose link failed isn't probed, and its supply is
already off.
---
 drivers/pci/pcie_dw_rockchip.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie_dw_rockchip.c b/drivers/pci/pcie_dw_rockchip.c
index 208aa30..d764762 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie_dw_rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie_dw_rockchip.c
@@ -486,6 +486,36 @@ rockchip_pcie_probe_err_init_port:
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/**
+ * rockchip_pcie_remove() - Put the slot back in reset before the OS starts
+ *
+ * @dev: A pointer to the device being operated on
+ *
+ * The OS expects to find the endpoint powered off or held in reset, and does
+ * its own power-up and link training. An endpoint left in L0 with PERST#
+ * released can fail to train again after the OS resets the controller (seen
+ * with the Motorcomm YT6801 on the Orange Pi 5 Pro), so assert PERST#, stop
+ * the LTSSM and remove the slot power.
+ *
+ * Return: 0
+ */
+static int rockchip_pcie_remove(struct udevice *dev)
+{
+	struct rk_pcie *priv = dev_get_priv(dev);
+	int ret;
+
+	if (dm_gpio_is_valid(&priv->rst_gpio))
+		dm_gpio_set_value(&priv->rst_gpio, 0);
+
+	rk_pcie_disable_ltssm(priv);
+
+	ret = regulator_set_enable_if_allowed(priv->vpcie3v3, false);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(dev, "failed to disable vpcie3v3 (ret=%d)\n", ret);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct dm_pci_ops rockchip_pcie_ops = {
 	.read_config	= pcie_dw_read_config,
 	.write_config	= pcie_dw_write_config,
@@ -503,5 +533,7 @@ U_BOOT_DRIVER(rockchip_dw_pcie) = {
 	.of_match		= rockchip_pcie_ids,
 	.ops			= &rockchip_pcie_ops,
 	.probe			= rockchip_pcie_probe,
+	.remove			= rockchip_pcie_remove,
 	.priv_auto		= sizeof(struct rk_pcie),
+	.flags			= DM_FLAG_OS_PREPARE,
 };
